$ maps the interval from $0$ to $1$ exclusive to the set containing the two numbers $0$ and $1$ only\"* is equivalent to the following symbolic notation:\n\n$\\,$ $h:(0,1)\\to \\{0,1\\}$\n\nHere, the domain of $h$ is $(0,1),$ and the codomain of $h$ is $\\{0,1\\}.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-7732c4e3-3161-5802-ab59-a7cdbdfc5997"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-7732c4e3-3161-5802-ab59-a7cdbdfc5997" :answer-field/id #uuid "7732c4e3-3161-5802-ab59-a7cdbdfc5997" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-541ffd3e-8a84-5a4f-bd1a-89894363b8da" :answer-field/choices ["answer-1035bbb6-7038-5b32-98d1-d43d0cee1aa3" "answer-43bcd4c6-a1f1-5472-bf3f-22916bfd9d61" "answer-541ffd3e-8a84-5a4f-bd1a-89894363b8da" "answer-e126d013-b0a4-5d2c-bf12-3c1d12a00d91" "answer-0b61bd54-1c7d-591e-939b-77de4327abc1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1035bbb6-7038-5b32-98d1-d43d0cee1aa3" :answer/id #uuid "1035bbb6-7038-5b32-98d1-d43d0cee1aa3" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:(0,1)\\to (0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-43bcd4c6-a1f1-5472-bf3f-22916bfd9d61" :answer/id #uuid "43bcd4c6-a1f1-5472-bf3f-22916bfd9d61" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:(0,1)\\to [0,1]" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-541ffd3e-8a84-5a4f-bd1a-89894363b8da" :answer/id #uuid "541ffd3e-8a84-5a4f-bd1a-89894363b8da" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:(0,1)\\to \\{0,1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-e126d013-b0a4-5d2c-bf12-3c1d12a00d91" :answer/id #uuid "e126d013-b0a4-5d2c-bf12-3c1d12a00d91" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:\\{0,1\\}\\to (0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0b61bd54-1c7d-591e-939b-77de4327abc1" :answer/id #uuid "0b61bd54-1c7d-591e-939b-77de4327abc1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:\\{0,1\\}\\to \\{0,1\\}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-97bd3e47-4a7d-51fe-87e4-ccb53cfbd7e2" :question/id #uuid "97bd3e47-4a7d-51fe-87e4-ccb53cfbd7e2" :question/math-academy-id "q-104941" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $h(x)=2{x}^{3}-3x?$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $h(x)=2{x}^{3}-3x$ means that the function $h$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $2{x}^{3}-3x$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\nh:x↦2{x}^{3}-3x.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-86cbd155-e168-55e6-b312-a580ef748d0a"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-86cbd155-e168-55e6-b312-a580ef748d0a" :answer-field/id #uuid "86cbd155-e168-55e6-b312-a580ef748d0a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-0aacc03f-d443-56a8-98ec-3789fe421eda" :answer-field/choices ["answer-a040e295-4426-5498-a1ec-eee2127b6a9e" "answer-783a5b80-d714-5773-9afd-24db9211e58b" "answer-554769e0-913b-5666-8b52-da7a146ba940" "answer-0aacc03f-d443-56a8-98ec-3789fe421eda" "answer-88ecda15-e589-5fe6-ad21-b805845401c9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-a040e295-4426-5498-a1ec-eee2127b6a9e" :answer/id #uuid "a040e295-4426-5498-a1ec-eee2127b6a9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:2{x}^{3}↦-3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-783a5b80-d714-5773-9afd-24db9211e58b" :answer/id #uuid "783a5b80-d714-5773-9afd-24db9211e58b" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:3x↦2{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-554769e0-913b-5666-8b52-da7a146ba940" :answer/id #uuid "554769e0-913b-5666-8b52-da7a146ba940" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:x↦-3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0aacc03f-d443-56a8-98ec-3789fe421eda" :answer/id #uuid "0aacc03f-d443-56a8-98ec-3789fe421eda" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:x↦2{x}^{3}-3x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-88ecda15-e589-5fe6-ad21-b805845401c9" :answer/id #uuid "88ecda15-e589-5fe6-ad21-b805845401c9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "h:x↦{x}^{3}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-366b227d-9c09-5249-bc0f-cb45c09620a0" :question/id #uuid "366b227d-9c09-5249-bc0f-cb45c09620a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-96819" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $g:x↦1?$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $g:x↦1$ means that the function $g$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $1$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\ng(x)=1.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/id #uuid "4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48" :answer-field/choices ["answer-77c0cb02-7243-5cb8-b055-248b6519b007" "answer-9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48" "answer-46c31195-e8be-52b6-93f1-fad3fbbeb5d7" "answer-0fb66b74-5889-5d7c-b8a3-82eac46f6c7e" "answer-dfc59561-87df-548e-b655-0825256d38e1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-77c0cb02-7243-5cb8-b055-248b6519b007" :answer/id #uuid "77c0cb02-7243-5cb8-b055-248b6519b007" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g(1)=x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48" :answer/id #uuid "9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g(x)=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-46c31195-e8be-52b6-93f1-fad3fbbeb5d7" :answer/id #uuid "46c31195-e8be-52b6-93f1-fad3fbbeb5d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "g(x)=1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0fb66b74-5889-5d7c-b8a3-82eac46f6c7e" :answer/id #uuid "0fb66b74-5889-5d7c-b8a3-82eac46f6c7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dfc59561-87df-548e-b655-0825256d38e1" :answer/id #uuid "dfc59561-87df-548e-b655-0825256d38e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x=1-x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-af103ef7-b89b-5289-9d5d-02c1e186f66e" :question/id #uuid "af103ef7-b89b-5289-9d5d-02c1e186f66e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104951" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6ac4933860ceea29b5892d1ea38685dd7d7fbb5e1a6a48cda45b48151b35aeb1.png)\n\nConsider the function $g:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The domain of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$\n\nII. The codomain of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$\n\nIII. The range of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $g:X\\to Y$ means that the function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $g$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X=\\{1,2,3\\},$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$\n\n- the range of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-1b5c1a5d-7ac0-5268-a351-1c74d654d1fd"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-1b5c1a5d-7ac0-5268-a351-1c74d654d1fd" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5c1a5d-7ac0-5268-a351-1c74d654d1fd" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-9ce61f7b-f3ab-56c7-96d3-2117a364b564" :answer-field/choices ["answer-0a37a47e-df4b-5a3b-b91d-251a23cdbc67" "answer-9ce61f7b-f3ab-56c7-96d3-2117a364b564" "answer-2bf5c615-bac0-5e6d-bed3-fad212104c62" "answer-84ab3d78-f997-5627-8d22-8f29bbd35fd7" "answer-1aa6843f-235e-55f5-a1d2-65b5255eca12"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-0a37a47e-df4b-5a3b-b91d-251a23cdbc67" :answer/id #uuid "0a37a47e-df4b-5a3b-b91d-251a23cdbc67" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-9ce61f7b-f3ab-56c7-96d3-2117a364b564" :answer/id #uuid "9ce61f7b-f3ab-56c7-96d3-2117a364b564" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-2bf5c615-bac0-5e6d-bed3-fad212104c62" :answer/id #uuid "2bf5c615-bac0-5e6d-bed3-fad212104c62" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-84ab3d78-f997-5627-8d22-8f29bbd35fd7" :answer/id #uuid "84ab3d78-f997-5627-8d22-8f29bbd35fd7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-1aa6843f-235e-55f5-a1d2-65b5255eca12" :answer/id #uuid "1aa6843f-235e-55f5-a1d2-65b5255eca12" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "question-1110805d-d0df-5ae9-af4b-5eeeabf99273" :question/id #uuid "1110805d-d0df-5ae9-af4b-5eeeabf99273" :question/math-academy-id "q-96828" :question/problem "![](images/1b/1b124a0e4439f1b35affa5a38f175a151cbbad88affb12738585da8280bacb23.png)\n\nConsider the function $f:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The domain of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\}$\n\nII. The codomain of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\}$\n\nIII. The range of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\}$" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $f$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X=\\{0,1\\},$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y=\\{0,1,2,3\\},$\n\n- the range of $f$ is $\\{0,1\\},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I and III only.\"" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["answer-field-20e843ef-72f4-5f6d-8133-a40e9b75a28b"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "answer-field-20e843ef-72f4-5f6d-8133-a40e9b75a28b" :answer-field/id #uuid "20e843ef-72f4-5f6d-8133-a40e9b75a28b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "answer-f4c0657f-5e00-5c2c-a966-63d4b0657c46" :answer-field/choices ["answer-fca7a609-f33e-5be9-ae87-737b69fc91e7" "answer-f4c0657f-5e00-5c2c-a966-63d4b0657c46" "answer-95810dec-fe98-5d62-b391-46de5d6c4ba9" "answer-66dc03df-3df9-5aee-880e-9b8893a454e7" "answer-dde14787-3b26-5768-9e9c-91acf6135f00"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "answer-fca7a609-f33e-5be9-ae87-737b69fc91e7" :answer/id #uuid "fca7a609-f33e-5be9-ae87-737b69fc91e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-f4c0657f-5e00-5c2c-a966-63d4b0657c46" :answer/id #uuid "f4c0657f-5e00-5c2c-a966-63d4b0657c46" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I and III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-95810dec-fe98-5d62-b391-46de5d6c4ba9" :answer/id #uuid "95810dec-fe98-5d62-b391-46de5d6c4ba9" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "I only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-66dc03df-3df9-5aee-880e-9b8893a454e7" :answer/id #uuid "66dc03df-3df9-5aee-880e-9b8893a454e7" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "II only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "answer-dde14787-3b26-5768-9e9c-91acf6135f00" :answer/id #uuid "dde14787-3b26-5768-9e9c-91acf6135f00" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "III only" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id 17592186172165 :activity/expected-seconds 420.0 :db/ensure [:activity/validate]}] "assertions" [[17592186171837 :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the codomain $[0,1]?$\n\nI. $p: \\{ 0, 1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}$\n\nII. $q: \\mathbb{R} \\to [ 0, 1 ]$\n\nIII. $r: [0,1] \\to [ 0, 1 )$"] [17592186171838 :question/problem "Which of the following is the correct symbolic notation for the sentence given below?\n\n$\\qquad$ *\"The function $g$ maps the set of rational numbers to the set $Y$.\"*\n\nI. $g:\\mathbb{Q} \\to Y$\n\nII. $g: Y \\to \\mathbb{Q}$\n\nIII. $g:\\mathbb{R} \\to Y$"] [17592186171839 :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $g(x)=x-x^3?$\n\nI. $g:x \\mapsto x-x^3$\n\nII. $g:x \\mapsto -x^3$\n\nIII. $g:-x \\mapsto x^3$"] [17592186171840 :question/problem "Which of the following is the correct interpretation of $g: \\{ -1,0,1 \\} \\to \\mathbb{R}?$\n\nI. The domain of $g$ is $\\{ -1,0,1 \\}$\n\nII. The codomain of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$\n\nIII. The range of $g$ is $\\mathbb{R}$"] ["question-03451249-6784-5494-bb32-85da8e4ecff7" :question/id #uuid "03451249-6784-5494-bb32-85da8e4ecff7"] ["question-03451249-6784-5494-bb32-85da8e4ecff7" :question/math-academy-id "q-96750"] ["question-03451249-6784-5494-bb32-85da8e4ecff7" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the domain $(0,2)?$\n\nI. $p:(0,2)\\to \\{0,2\\}$\n\nII. $q:R\\to (0,2)$\n\nIII. $r:(0,2)\\to R$"] ["question-03451249-6784-5494-bb32-85da8e4ecff7" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is $(0,2),$ the interval from $0$ to $2$ (not including $0$ nor $2$).\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $(0,2),$ the interval from $0$ to $2$ (not including $0$ nor $2$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and III only.\""] ["question-03451249-6784-5494-bb32-85da8e4ecff7" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977" :answer-field/id #uuid "57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977"] ["answer-87f28eff-b85c-51e4-bfdb-402ad594d1d7" :answer/id #uuid "87f28eff-b85c-51e4-bfdb-402ad594d1d7"] ["answer-87f28eff-b85c-51e4-bfdb-402ad594d1d7" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-87f28eff-b85c-51e4-bfdb-402ad594d1d7" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-86d8385b-658f-55ab-818a-9655645ea8ca" :answer/id #uuid "86d8385b-658f-55ab-818a-9655645ea8ca"] ["answer-86d8385b-658f-55ab-818a-9655645ea8ca" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-86d8385b-658f-55ab-818a-9655645ea8ca" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-cef5775c-2fbc-5e17-99c4-f04975560bc1" :answer/id #uuid "cef5775c-2fbc-5e17-99c4-f04975560bc1"] ["answer-cef5775c-2fbc-5e17-99c4-f04975560bc1" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-cef5775c-2fbc-5e17-99c4-f04975560bc1" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-4ee7dff7-3395-58fe-8812-401b24d3c95c" :answer/id #uuid "4ee7dff7-3395-58fe-8812-401b24d3c95c"] ["answer-4ee7dff7-3395-58fe-8812-401b24d3c95c" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-4ee7dff7-3395-58fe-8812-401b24d3c95c" :answer/value "I, II, and III"] ["answer-02afc777-71c7-54a7-ba97-7bbbfed64a98" :answer/id #uuid "02afc777-71c7-54a7-ba97-7bbbfed64a98"] ["answer-02afc777-71c7-54a7-ba97-7bbbfed64a98" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-02afc777-71c7-54a7-ba97-7bbbfed64a98" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977" :answer-field/correct "answer-86d8385b-658f-55ab-818a-9655645ea8ca"] ["answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977" :answer-field/choices "answer-87f28eff-b85c-51e4-bfdb-402ad594d1d7"] ["answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977" :answer-field/choices "answer-86d8385b-658f-55ab-818a-9655645ea8ca"] ["answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977" :answer-field/choices "answer-cef5775c-2fbc-5e17-99c4-f04975560bc1"] ["answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977" :answer-field/choices "answer-4ee7dff7-3395-58fe-8812-401b24d3c95c"] ["answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977" :answer-field/choices "answer-02afc777-71c7-54a7-ba97-7bbbfed64a98"] ["question-03451249-6784-5494-bb32-85da8e4ecff7" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-57c4d1e2-df8c-582b-885f-5ecfb77ad977"] [17592186172031 :knowledge-point/questions "question-03451249-6784-5494-bb32-85da8e4ecff7"] [17592186172627 :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the codomain $[0,3)?$\n\nI. $p:\\{0,3\\}\\to R$\n\nII. $q:R\\to [0,3)$\n\nIII. $r:[0,3)\\to \\{0,3\\}$"] [17592186172627 :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $[0,3),$ the interval from $0$ to $3$ (including $0$ but not including $3$).\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $\\{0,3\\},$ the set containing the two numbers $0$ and $3$ only.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\""] [17592186172627 :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] [17592186171387 :answer-field/correct 17592186171392] ["question-5328fc24-dd2c-524e-ade9-b248f99c64bf" :question/id #uuid "5328fc24-dd2c-524e-ade9-b248f99c64bf"] ["question-5328fc24-dd2c-524e-ade9-b248f99c64bf" :question/math-academy-id "q-96742"] ["question-5328fc24-dd2c-524e-ade9-b248f99c64bf" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the codomain $R?$\n\nI. $p:[0,1]\\to R$\n\nII. $q:R\\to R$\n\nIII. $r:[0,1]\\to [0,1]$"] ["question-5328fc24-dd2c-524e-ade9-b248f99c64bf" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The codomain of $p$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $q$ is $R,$ the set of real numbers.\n\n- The codomain of $r$ is $[0,1],$ the interval from $0$ to $1$ (including $0$ and $1$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""] ["question-5328fc24-dd2c-524e-ade9-b248f99c64bf" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785" :answer-field/id #uuid "0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785"] ["answer-94fa83da-80c7-5f55-9464-39fa5c58c114" :answer/id #uuid "94fa83da-80c7-5f55-9464-39fa5c58c114"] ["answer-94fa83da-80c7-5f55-9464-39fa5c58c114" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-94fa83da-80c7-5f55-9464-39fa5c58c114" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-02c9c58a-a214-5eba-901a-bdc452270c65" :answer/id #uuid "02c9c58a-a214-5eba-901a-bdc452270c65"] ["answer-02c9c58a-a214-5eba-901a-bdc452270c65" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-02c9c58a-a214-5eba-901a-bdc452270c65" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-c329a7b2-7848-5e75-84a5-25bcb45d6cff" :answer/id #uuid "c329a7b2-7848-5e75-84a5-25bcb45d6cff"] ["answer-c329a7b2-7848-5e75-84a5-25bcb45d6cff" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-c329a7b2-7848-5e75-84a5-25bcb45d6cff" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-d81158c2-eba9-59f7-9367-d11127d5d5a0" :answer/id #uuid "d81158c2-eba9-59f7-9367-d11127d5d5a0"] ["answer-d81158c2-eba9-59f7-9367-d11127d5d5a0" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-d81158c2-eba9-59f7-9367-d11127d5d5a0" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-8f698421-325f-5fcb-a32f-80af1dd9ee46" :answer/id #uuid "8f698421-325f-5fcb-a32f-80af1dd9ee46"] ["answer-8f698421-325f-5fcb-a32f-80af1dd9ee46" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-8f698421-325f-5fcb-a32f-80af1dd9ee46" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785" :answer-field/correct "answer-94fa83da-80c7-5f55-9464-39fa5c58c114"] ["answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785" :answer-field/choices "answer-94fa83da-80c7-5f55-9464-39fa5c58c114"] ["answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785" :answer-field/choices "answer-02c9c58a-a214-5eba-901a-bdc452270c65"] ["answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785" :answer-field/choices "answer-c329a7b2-7848-5e75-84a5-25bcb45d6cff"] ["answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785" :answer-field/choices "answer-d81158c2-eba9-59f7-9367-d11127d5d5a0"] ["answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785" :answer-field/choices "answer-8f698421-325f-5fcb-a32f-80af1dd9ee46"] ["question-5328fc24-dd2c-524e-ade9-b248f99c64bf" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-0696edc7-2d9c-5594-b819-83895889d785"] [17592186172031 :knowledge-point/questions "question-5328fc24-dd2c-524e-ade9-b248f99c64bf"] ["question-f312482e-bbe1-5f40-a816-ce63ddb8cbac" :question/id #uuid "f312482e-bbe1-5f40-a816-ce63ddb8cbac"] ["question-f312482e-bbe1-5f40-a816-ce63ddb8cbac" :question/math-academy-id "q-96746"] ["question-f312482e-bbe1-5f40-a816-ce63ddb8cbac" :question/problem "Which of the following functions has the domain $(-2,0)?$\n\nI. $p:(-2,0)\\to \\{-2,0\\}$\n\nII. $q:(-2,0)\\to (-2,0)$\n\nIII. $r:[-2,0)\\to (0,2)$"] ["question-f312482e-bbe1-5f40-a816-ce63ddb8cbac" :question/worked-solution "The notation $f:X\\to Y$ means that the function $f$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $f$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $f$ is $Y.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our functions.\n\n- The domain of $p$ is $(-2,0),$ the interval from $-2$ to $0$ (not including $-2$ nor $0$).\n\n- The domain of $q$ is $(-2,0),$ the interval from $-2$ to $0$ (not including $-2$ nor $0$).\n\n- The domain of $r$ is $[-2,0),$ the interval from $-2$ to $0$ (including $-2$ but not including $0$).\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I and II only.\""] ["question-f312482e-bbe1-5f40-a816-ce63ddb8cbac" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-550f1c25-0293-5be1-ae65-eb50dd02286b" :answer-field/id #uuid "550f1c25-0293-5be1-ae65-eb50dd02286b"] ["answer-3d23e7c9-40ba-5b54-b02d-21430ba708f2" :answer/id #uuid "3d23e7c9-40ba-5b54-b02d-21430ba708f2"] ["answer-3d23e7c9-40ba-5b54-b02d-21430ba708f2" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-3d23e7c9-40ba-5b54-b02d-21430ba708f2" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-884b94a9-d6b2-5eeb-b350-6ea73296ca6a" :answer/id #uuid "884b94a9-d6b2-5eeb-b350-6ea73296ca6a"] ["answer-884b94a9-d6b2-5eeb-b350-6ea73296ca6a" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-884b94a9-d6b2-5eeb-b350-6ea73296ca6a" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-3e4753ac-ec9a-5118-9d5f-497d9fdf772e" :answer/id #uuid "3e4753ac-ec9a-5118-9d5f-497d9fdf772e"] ["answer-3e4753ac-ec9a-5118-9d5f-497d9fdf772e" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-3e4753ac-ec9a-5118-9d5f-497d9fdf772e" :answer/value "II and III only"] ["answer-4b0dea5d-3507-56bb-8583-68afdd27c73c" :answer/id #uuid "4b0dea5d-3507-56bb-8583-68afdd27c73c"] ["answer-4b0dea5d-3507-56bb-8583-68afdd27c73c" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-4b0dea5d-3507-56bb-8583-68afdd27c73c" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-64b5696e-2731-5353-9177-5de35368dca6" :answer/id #uuid "64b5696e-2731-5353-9177-5de35368dca6"] ["answer-64b5696e-2731-5353-9177-5de35368dca6" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-64b5696e-2731-5353-9177-5de35368dca6" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-550f1c25-0293-5be1-ae65-eb50dd02286b" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-550f1c25-0293-5be1-ae65-eb50dd02286b" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-550f1c25-0293-5be1-ae65-eb50dd