my-id "q-96819"] ["question-366b227d-9c09-5249-bc0f-cb45c09620a0" :question/problem "Which of the following is equivalent to $g:x↦1?$"] ["question-366b227d-9c09-5249-bc0f-cb45c09620a0" :question/worked-solution "The notation $g:x↦1$ means that the function $g$ maps the element $x$ in the domain to $1$ in the codomain. This can also be written as\n\n$$\ng(x)=1.\n$$"] ["question-366b227d-9c09-5249-bc0f-cb45c09620a0" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/id #uuid "4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f"] ["answer-77c0cb02-7243-5cb8-b055-248b6519b007" :answer/id #uuid "77c0cb02-7243-5cb8-b055-248b6519b007"] ["answer-77c0cb02-7243-5cb8-b055-248b6519b007" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-77c0cb02-7243-5cb8-b055-248b6519b007" :answer/value "g(1)=x"] ["answer-9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48" :answer/id #uuid "9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48"] ["answer-9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48" :answer/value "g(x)=1"] ["answer-46c31195-e8be-52b6-93f1-fad3fbbeb5d7" :answer/id #uuid "46c31195-e8be-52b6-93f1-fad3fbbeb5d7"] ["answer-46c31195-e8be-52b6-93f1-fad3fbbeb5d7" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-46c31195-e8be-52b6-93f1-fad3fbbeb5d7" :answer/value "g(x)=1-x"] ["answer-0fb66b74-5889-5d7c-b8a3-82eac46f6c7e" :answer/id #uuid "0fb66b74-5889-5d7c-b8a3-82eac46f6c7e"] ["answer-0fb66b74-5889-5d7c-b8a3-82eac46f6c7e" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-0fb66b74-5889-5d7c-b8a3-82eac46f6c7e" :answer/value "x=1"] ["answer-dfc59561-87df-548e-b655-0825256d38e1" :answer/id #uuid "dfc59561-87df-548e-b655-0825256d38e1"] ["answer-dfc59561-87df-548e-b655-0825256d38e1" :answer/type :answer.type/math] ["answer-dfc59561-87df-548e-b655-0825256d38e1" :answer/value "x=1-x"] ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio] ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/correct "answer-9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48"] ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/choices "answer-77c0cb02-7243-5cb8-b055-248b6519b007"] ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/choices "answer-9b72735d-5c63-52e9-b20e-94395a94fb48"] ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/choices "answer-46c31195-e8be-52b6-93f1-fad3fbbeb5d7"] ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/choices "answer-0fb66b74-5889-5d7c-b8a3-82eac46f6c7e"] ["answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f" :answer-field/choices "answer-dfc59561-87df-548e-b655-0825256d38e1"] ["question-366b227d-9c09-5249-bc0f-cb45c09620a0" :question/answer-fields "answer-field-4eb70082-dd07-5801-b800-bc795ad3795f"] [17592186172033 :knowledge-point/questions "question-366b227d-9c09-5249-bc0f-cb45c09620a0"] ["question-af103ef7-b89b-5289-9d5d-02c1e186f66e" :question/id #uuid "af103ef7-b89b-5289-9d5d-02c1e186f66e"] ["question-af103ef7-b89b-5289-9d5d-02c1e186f66e" :question/math-academy-id "q-104951"] ["question-af103ef7-b89b-5289-9d5d-02c1e186f66e" :question/problem "![](images/6a/6ac4933860ceea29b5892d1ea38685dd7d7fbb5e1a6a48cda45b48151b35aeb1.png)\n\nConsider the function $g:X\\to Y$ given by the mapping diagram shown above. Which of the following statements are true?\n\nI. The domain of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$\n\nII. The codomain of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$\n\nIII. The range of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\}$"] ["question-af103ef7-b89b-5289-9d5d-02c1e186f66e" :question/worked-solution "The notation $g:X\\to Y$ means that the function $g$ maps the set $X$ to the set $Y.$ In this case,\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X,$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y.$\n\nThe range of $g$ is the subset of the codomain that contains all values $y\\in Y$ that are mapped to by at least one element $x\\in X.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's inspect our diagram:\n\n- the domain of $g$ is $X=\\{1,2,3\\},$\n\n- the codomain of $g$ is $Y=\\{1,2,3,4\\},$\n\n- the range of $g$ is $\\{1,2,3\\},$ the subset of elements of $Y$ that have at least one incoming arrow.\n\nAs a result, statements I and III are true, while statement II is false.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer \"I and III only.\""] ["question-af103ef7-b89b-5289-9d5d-02c1e186f66e" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy] ["answer-field-1b5c1a5d-7ac0-5268-a351-1c74d654d1fd" :answer-field/id #uuid "1b5c1a5d-7ac0-5268-a351-1c74d654d1fd"] ["answer-0a37a47e-df4b-5a3b-b91d-251a23cdbc67" :answer/id #uuid "0a37a47e-df4b-5a3b-b91d-251a23cdbc67"] ["answer-0a37a47e-df4b-5a3b-b91d-251a23cdbc67" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-0a37a47e-df4b-5a3b-b91d-251a23cdbc67" :answer/value "I and II only"] ["answer-9ce61f7b-f3ab-56c7-96d3-2117a364b564" :answer/id #uuid "9ce61f7b-f3ab-56c7-96d3-2117a364b564"] ["answer-9ce61f7b-f3ab-56c7-96d3-2117a364b564" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-9ce61f7b-f3ab-56c7-96d3-2117a364b564" :answer/value "I and III only"] ["answer-2bf5c615-bac0-5e6d-bed3-fad212104c62" :answer/id #uuid "2bf5c615-bac0-5e6d-bed3-fad212104c62"] ["answer-2bf5c615-bac0-5e6d-bed3-fad212104c62" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-2bf5c615-bac0-5e6d-bed3-fad212104c62" :answer/value "I only"] ["answer-84ab3d78-f997-5627-8d22-8f29bbd35fd7" :answer/id #uuid "84ab3d78-f997-5627-8d22-8f29bbd35fd7"] ["answer-84ab3d78-f997-5627-8d22-8f29bbd35fd7" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-84ab3d78-f997-5627-8d22-8f29bbd35fd7" :answer/value "II only"] ["answer-1aa6843f-235e-55f5-a1d2-65b5255eca12" :answer/id #uuid "1aa6843f-235e-55f5-a1d2-65b5255eca12"] ["answer-1aa6843f-235e-55f5-a1d2-65b5255eca12" :answer/type :answer.type/text] ["answer-1aa6843f-235e-55f5-a1d2-65b5255eca12" :answer/value "III only"] ["answer-field-1b5c1a5d-7ac0-5268-a351-1c74d654d1fd" :answer-field/key "selection"] ["answer-field-1b5c1a5d-7ac0-5268-a351-1c74d654d1fd" :answer-field/type :ans